Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:14:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770/hp39gii: F2 types a minus, NAND bus state dump

- F2 (matrix 1,1) emits "-", and the hint bar now reads
  "F1=SPC F2=- UP/DN=SCRL L/R=PAGE".
- Bound every APBH DEBUG2 byte-counter wait as well, so no NAND read
  path can spin forever.
- After the first page read, dump ECC_FIN, the channel semaphore, AHB/APB
  byte counters, ECC8_CTRL/STATUS1, APBH_CTRL0 and the accumulated ECC
  result, plus the clock registers before init.

Hardware currently reads back all 0x00 (the page buffer is never
written), so the ECC/DMA transfer is not completing.
